1
00:00:06,060 --> 00:00:07,770
First, there was darkness.

2
00:00:07,820 --> 00:00:10,890
Then… the earth pushed me up.

3
00:00:10,940 --> 00:00:15,370
A mace in my hand. A roar on my lips. The same fire in my chest.

4
00:00:15,420 --> 00:00:20,890
I remembered everything — Shumbha's command, the marching armies, Aindri's thunderbolt.

5
00:00:21,020 --> 00:00:22,970
I knew who I was.

6
00:00:23,580 --> 00:00:25,690
I am Raktabija.

7
00:00:26,920 --> 00:00:33,110
I remember — Chanda and Munda had fallen, and Shumbha sent every clan into battle.

8
00:00:33,160 --> 00:00:38,150
The Devi drew her bowstring, and its twang filled earth and sky.

9
00:00:38,200 --> 00:00:40,150
The lion roared. The bell rang.

10
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:43,150
And Kali's roar swallowed every other sound.

11
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:44,030
Then they came.

12
00:00:44,080 --> 00:00:47,270
Brahmani. Maheshvari. Kaumari. Vaishnavi.

13
00:00:47,320 --> 00:00:49,550
Varahi. Narasimhi. Aindri.

14
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:52,550
And the Devi's own power — Shivaduti.

15
00:00:53,480 --> 00:00:56,510
Our armies fell on them — and broke.

16
00:00:56,560 --> 00:01:00,630
That's when I stepped forward. Raktabija stepped forward.

17
00:01:00,680 --> 00:01:07,110
Because I had what no one else had — wherever my blood falls, I rise again.

18
00:01:07,160 --> 00:01:13,190
Aindri's thunderbolt struck my brow. Blood flowed… and I rose. Here, from this very earth.

19
00:01:13,880 --> 00:01:18,310
Strike me. The more you strike, the more of me there will be.

20
00:01:19,280 --> 00:01:20,990
That's when I saw him.

21
00:01:21,040 --> 00:01:28,870
Beside me — my face. My mace. My own laugh, the one that had just left my lips.

22
00:01:28,920 --> 00:01:32,590
He saw me too. And in his eyes was the same question —

23
00:01:32,790 --> 00:01:34,110
"Who are you?"

24
00:01:35,200 --> 00:01:39,350
Then another. Then ten. Then I stopped counting.

25
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:49,230
And then — through the crowd, at the very front — I saw him. Raktabija. The thunderbolt's wound on his brow, still bleeding.

26
00:01:49,280 --> 00:01:52,590
I touched my brow. There was no wound.

27
00:01:52,800 --> 00:01:58,770
That wound was mine. I remembered its pain. But it was not on my body.

28
00:01:58,820 --> 00:02:03,590
Because I was not his body. I was his blood.

29
00:02:03,640 --> 00:02:10,910
His memories, his anger, his pride — all of it was in me. But I had been born a moment ago.

30
00:02:10,960 --> 00:02:13,059
I was not Raktabija.

31
00:02:13,109 --> 00:02:16,110
I was one drop of Raktabija.

32
00:02:22,680 --> 00:02:24,550
Then came Vaishnavi's discus.

33
00:02:24,600 --> 00:02:30,150
Its wound was deep. And from the blood that flowed… we rose in thousands.

34
00:02:30,200 --> 00:02:35,550
Aindri's mace. Kaumari's spear. Varahi's sword. Maheshvari's trident.

35
00:02:35,600 --> 00:02:42,350
With every blow, more Raktabijas rose from the earth… until the whole world was full of us.

36
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:49,857
I felt every birth — a low hum in my veins. As if someone were calling my name, again and again…

37
00:02:49,907 --> 00:02:53,510
…and each time, the name became a little less mine.

38
00:02:53,560 --> 00:02:59,257
A thousand faces. Identical. One memory, one rage, one "I".

39
00:02:59,307 --> 00:03:01,030
So who am I?

40
00:03:02,040 --> 00:03:08,910
Only one thing set me apart — the mark on my chest of the earth I had pushed through to rise.

41
00:03:08,960 --> 00:03:13,030
As if the earth had touched me… so that someone, at least, would know me.

42
00:03:13,080 --> 00:03:16,910
Above, the gods' faces had fallen. I saw their fear.

43
00:03:16,960 --> 00:03:19,830
In that moment, we thought we had won.

44
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:26,230
We all ran together — the same roar, the same mace, the same stride.

45
00:03:26,280 --> 00:03:32,230
And beside me was the same one — the first one I had seen. The one with my question in his eyes.

46
00:03:32,280 --> 00:03:35,270
Kaumari's spear flashed… and he stopped.

47
00:03:35,400 --> 00:03:39,590
He fell — and kept turning into dust, as if he had never been.

48
00:03:39,800 --> 00:03:43,350
I held him. His weight… was exactly mine.

49
00:03:43,400 --> 00:03:49,110
He tried to say something. Perhaps the same thing — "I am Raktabija." But the words never finished.

50
00:03:49,160 --> 00:03:51,870
And then I understood why we were here.

51
00:03:51,920 --> 00:03:54,510
We were not warriors. We were a wall.

52
00:03:54,560 --> 00:04:01,910
Every drop a shield. And every shield made to break — so that he, standing at the front, could stay standing.

53
00:04:01,960 --> 00:04:07,030
I was born so that I could fall. So that another could rise.

54
00:04:07,080 --> 00:04:11,390
And the strangest part? Even knowing this… my hand did not let go of the mace.

55
00:04:11,440 --> 00:04:18,790
Because I was made of that same pride. The pride that had seized Indra's heaven, and seized the gods' share of the sacrifice.

56
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:22,950
I was not innocent. I was only new.

57
00:04:24,720 --> 00:04:27,070
Then everything slowed.

58
00:04:27,360 --> 00:04:38,750
Seeing the gods in despair, Chandika said something to Kali. I was far away. But the voice came not through the air — it came through the blood, as if it rang inside me.

59
00:04:38,867 --> 00:04:48,270
"Chamunda… open wide your mouth. Take in the blood my weapon spills — and the asuras born of it.

60
00:04:48,320 --> 00:04:55,110
Roam the battlefield, and devour them. Then this asura, drained of blood, will perish…

61
00:04:55,160 --> 00:04:57,217
…and no more will be born."

62
00:04:57,267 --> 00:05:03,310
"No more will be born." In that one sentence was written the end of thousands like me.

63
00:05:05,280 --> 00:05:05,950
She came.

64
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:12,030
First her shadow came — so vast that even the sun's last ray was lost in it.

65
00:05:12,080 --> 00:05:16,750
The one who had felled Chanda and Munda. Chamunda.

66
00:05:16,880 --> 00:05:23,430
The Devi struck Raktabija with her dart. Blood flowed — but this time, it never reached the ground.

67
00:05:23,480 --> 00:05:26,190
Kali's mouth took it in mid-air.

68
00:05:26,240 --> 00:05:28,270
And that hum in my veins —

69
00:05:28,702 --> 00:05:29,550
— stopped.

70
00:05:30,800 --> 00:05:33,350
For the first time, the earth was silent.

71
00:05:33,400 --> 00:05:36,310
No new birth. No new "I".

72
00:05:36,360 --> 00:05:39,670
Those who were born inside her mouth, she swallowed there and then.

73
00:05:39,720 --> 00:05:42,950
Then she began to roam the battlefield — among all of us.

74
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:47,950
And we — thousands of Raktabijas — one by one, went into that darkness.

75
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:50,430
I should have been afraid. I was.

76
00:05:50,480 --> 00:05:54,830
But under the fear was something else, something I felt for the first time…

77
00:05:55,017 --> 00:05:55,950
…relief.

78
00:05:57,080 --> 00:06:01,070
Raktabija raised his mace one last time, and struck Chandika.

79
00:06:01,120 --> 00:06:03,510
It caused her no pain at all.

80
00:06:04,940 --> 00:06:14,330
Dart, thunderbolt, arrows, swords, spears — the Devi's weapons rained on him… and Chamunda drank every drop.

81
00:06:14,380 --> 00:06:18,530
And then, drained of blood, Raktabija fell to the earth.

82
00:06:18,580 --> 00:06:23,050
The one I was a memory of… the one whose blood I was… had fallen.

83
00:06:23,100 --> 00:06:25,090
And I was still standing.

84
00:06:25,140 --> 00:06:30,530
For the first time, no one else was speaking inside me. Not his rage. Not his command.

85
00:06:30,580 --> 00:06:33,650
Only one question was left — and it was my own.

86
00:06:33,700 --> 00:06:38,490
If I am not Raktabija… then in these last moments, what am I?

87
00:06:40,720 --> 00:06:42,590
She was before me.

88
00:06:42,640 --> 00:06:48,590
I set down my mace. It was my first choice. Perhaps my only one.

89
00:06:48,640 --> 00:06:54,030
I looked up. In her eyes was the terror the three worlds tremble before.

90
00:06:54,080 --> 00:06:56,670
But beneath it… there was something else as well.

91
00:06:56,720 --> 00:07:02,670
Relentlessness in battle. And compassion in the heart. Both at once. In the same eyes.

92
00:07:19,720 --> 00:07:21,190
And she looked at me.

93
00:07:21,240 --> 00:07:24,950
Not at Raktabija. Not at one face among a thousand.

94
00:07:25,080 --> 00:07:26,030
At me.

95
00:07:26,480 --> 00:07:31,350
The one who, moments ago, did not even know his own name — the Mother knew him.

96
00:07:31,400 --> 00:07:35,630
I lived for a few minutes. As long as a battle. As long as a drop.

97
00:07:35,680 --> 00:07:41,454
They say the Devi could burn the asuras to ash with a single glance. Yet she raises her weapons —

98
00:07:41,504 --> 00:07:45,870
— so that, purified by them, even her enemies may reach the higher worlds.

99
00:07:45,920 --> 00:07:52,750
I do not know if I will reach that far. But in that moment, for the first time… I was not afraid to fall.

100
00:07:52,800 --> 00:07:54,470
I was not Raktabija.

101
00:07:54,520 --> 00:07:56,630
I was a drop that fell…

102
00:07:56,680 --> 00:08:00,270
…and the Mother caught it before it touched the ground.
